{
  "answer": {
    "answer_text": "An NHS prescription in England costs **£9.90 per item**. That charge stays the same for the 2026/27 financial year, the government has announced.\n\nIf you need a lot of medicines, a prepayment certificate (PPC) can save you money:\n- A 3-month PPC costs £32.05, and a 12-month PPC costs £114.50.\n- An HRT PPC is £19.80 a year.\n- A 3-month PPC saves money if you need 4 or more items in 3 months. A 12-month PPC saves money at 12 or more items in a year.\n\nMany people are exempt and pay nothing. Charges also only apply in England: Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland have free prescriptions.",
